  "description": "Discontinued, superseded by Gen6. This page is kept as an archive record for owners and for anyone researching an older Cotic BFe.\n\nYears of production: 2017-2019\n\nThis is the 5th generation BFe, the first with Longshot geometry. See the BFe archive, and the current BFe.\n\nThe BFe is our trail bashing, downhill thrashing, jump park smashing, enduro winning, do-it-all fun machine.\n\nRight from its introduction in 2005, the BFe has always been the tearaway of the Cotic family: the Soul's stockier, rowdier younger brother. You know the one, loads of fun, but a bit on the wild side? That's the BFe.\n\nNew for 2018 was an Extra Small (XS) size so everyone could enjoy some hardtail shredding, and a gorgeous Champagne metallic paint option.\n\nRe-invented for its 5th generation, the BFe took the biggest step forward in geometry and features since it was first launched. During our focus on the droplink full suspension bikes over the previous couple of years, we got to wondering what a hardtail with Rocket style geometry would be like. The answer was the new BFe: longer, slacker, lower and more capable than ever. And fast. So, so fast!\n\nThe BFe has always been a diverse beast. Size down and mount up with a 120mm fork and it is suited to smashing the dirt jumps, local BMX or 4X track, with geometry that makes it easy to throw down style and tricks like there is no tomorrow.\n\nWith a 140mm fork and sized with room to move, the BFe turns into the dream trail bike which climbs nearly as fast as it descends, whilst keeping a huge grin on your face.\n\nWhen suited up with a 150mm-160mm fork, the BFe has no qualms about keeping up with your mates on their big fancy full-sus rigs at the enduros. It can comfortably handle those big forks, so you can get hooning on near enough any downhill track you choose.\n\nThe frame is based around a Reynolds 853 down tube, which allows us to keep massive strength where it matters most, whilst keeping weight down. The rest of the frame is our own Fm heat treated double butted cromoly steel, which helps keep strength and value high throughout. There are no corners cut: all the usual Cotic features of Ovalform top tube, oversized plug welded seat tube, wishbone stays, Syntace thru axle dropouts, stealth seatpost routing and a taper steerer compatible head tube are present and correct.\n\nThrow in massive clearance for latest generation wide rubber (27.5 x 2.6\" or 26 x 3.0\" tyres) and you'll be taking on all terrain in your stride, giving you the confidence to ride faster and be buzzing to do \"just another run\".\n\nTrail, enduro, 4X, downhill, bike parks: the BFe would do it all. BFe: Burly Iron.",
